Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/BrucePerens/hams_open/tree/main/hardware/grub_large_console

Package: grub-large-console
Architecture: all
Depends: grub-common, fonts-dejavu-core, ${misc:Depends}
Description: readable GRUB text on high-resolution screens
 GRUB draws its menu with a small fixed font, which is microscopic on a
 high-resolution panel.  This package reads the screen's native mode and
 generates a monospace font sized for roughly 80 columns by 24 rows on that
 screen, then points GRUB at it (a drop-in in /etc/default/grub.d) and runs
 update-grub.
 .
 Run "dpkg-reconfigure grub-large-console" after changing the display.
